Also at base, two more migrations move demo data through the same production
path: `5302128_role_catalog_expansion.sql` (a guarded demo-user block) and
`5302406_device_profiles.sql` (an UNGUARDED demo insert referencing the five
demo org ids). Both are gated by the same fix so the migration chain stays
valid on an empty database.

--- Fix applied ---
Replaced the "skip only if a production-like domain exists" heuristic in all
demo-seeding blocks with an explicit opt-in setting that defaults OFF:
  coalesce(current_setting('app.seed_demo', true), '') <> 'true'  ->  skip
Demo data now only loads when an operator explicitly enables it on a disposable
database (`alter database postgres set app.seed_demo = 'true';`). Local/E2E
`supabase db reset` still gets demo data from supabase/seeds/ (config.toml
[db.seed]), which run AFTER migrations. Files changed:
  supabase/migrations/5302119_demo_test_data.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302120_demo_module_data.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302121_demo_permission_edge_cases.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302123_demo_expanded_test_data.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302126_demo_worker_admin_coverage.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302128_role_catalog_expansion.sql
  supabase/migrations/5302406_device_profiles.sql

